  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;WEST AFRICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"West Africa is the region where the impact of climate change adaptation strategies on major crop yields is being assessed."</data>
      <data key="d2">a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATE CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Climate Change refers to the global phenomenon being addressed by the study, encompassing long-term shifts in temperatures and weather patterns due to human activities. It is a significant challenge for European livestock farming systems and impacts the yield and quality of European pastures. Climate Change is a central factor being studied in relation to tropical forests and, as a driving force, influences observed impacts on pollinators and tropical forests. Furthermore, it is the overarching environmental factor being investigated for its impact on a wide range of biological responses, including entomofauna distribution and abundance. The study of soil greenhouse gas fluxes is conducted within the context of Climate Change, highlighting the urgency of addressing this global issue, which includes alterations to environmental conditions, temperature, precipitation, and sea level.</data>
      <data key="d2">074b514b13d7fb732f7b2d8c00ec86bf,0e9c51f0e77cb7de623b5321b1975f1f,1f78616e6b65c9d016f9135e80758760,2b12ab6446d27607dd49219a456101d4,38ecd3b1f92e1c892d2086389566727e,40779d37dc6109c75c8ee8b81e777ffd,450ffbd59469d6da2dc5f32d199c5cd4,489357f7d77d21e208a06c332667b572,522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b,5dfbc10ef83070bbc81c332433747ef1,823c08dda0ef4bfee3fc54f016f7144e,8aeb638681f18df88f7a686b5a726c57,98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40,9e4056573475eaed647bd42b3b7ee26f,a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d,a5f7a50e301f77d88594300e5156f8f7,abda80eba504d6eb74af56b968bdda51,c67d047c45f8ba0a6e4722e26278e2b0,ef97b32fe243a50a490343e1874e561c,fcaf7506797fe15f7c0168be7d966591,fd80116ab9523ba9722fe86c6f42536c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROP YIELDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Crop Yields refers to the amount of crops produced. It also represents the increase in grain production achieved through organic conservation agriculture. Furthermore, Crop Yields is a metric being affected by climate change and adaptation strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9,a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d,c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADAPTATION STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adaptation Strategies are the measures being implemented to mitigate the negative impacts of climate change on crop yields."</data>
      <data key="d2">a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YIELDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yields are the metric being affected by climate change and adaptation strategies."</data>
      <data key="d2">a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCREASED FERTILISER USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPTIMIZED PLANTING DATES AND CULTIVARS WITH LONGER CROP CYCLE DURATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">a24c97db84957739fb0a983dd2c54c5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHANE (CH4)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Methane (CH4) is being measured and analyzed as a greenhouse gas. It is also recognized as an important anthropogenic greenhouse gas.</data>
      <data key="d2">273d381e70152fe67e5be227d158799d,c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOREST SOILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Forest Soils" refers to the soil environment where methane uptake is being studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">074b514b13d7fb732f7b2d8c00ec86bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Methane is a key chemical compound that is being measured as part of a study examining fluxes. It is identified as a central focus of the research question and is recognized as a greenhouse gas. Specifically, the study investigates the uptake of methane, with this uptake being a primary focus of the research. Afforestation is noted as influencing the gas&#8217;s uptake.</data>
      <data key="d2">074b514b13d7fb732f7b2d8c00ec86bf,81f63213c44b6a3bf615b9e54ee71282,b4d1a20395e31d77608ee4c3ad9117a2,d1f1904224d30c046fea452f4ffd9353</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL MOISTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil Moisture is identified as a key factor influencing CH4 uptake."</data>
      <data key="d2">074b514b13d7fb732f7b2d8c00ec86bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH4 UPTAKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">CH4 Uptake is the primary process being studied, and its relationship to climate change. Specifically, CH4 uptake refers to the process of methane being absorbed by the soil.</data>
      <data key="d2">074b514b13d7fb732f7b2d8c00ec86bf,d1f1904224d30c046fea452f4ffd9353</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCESS-BASED MODELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Process-Based Models are suggested as a necessary approach for predicting ecosystem responses to climate change."</data>
      <data key="d2">074b514b13d7fb732f7b2d8c00ec86bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN ENRICHMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogen Enrichment is a key factor influencing belowground carbon dynamics in terrestrial ecosystems. It refers to the process of increasing nitrogen levels in the soil, and is the cause of observed changes within these ecosystems. Specifically, Nitrogen Enrichment involves adding nitrogen to the soil.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c710480b85fa68cc11d1a7b09585383,4caecf1d3bbc05db831098f8d95eeda3,ca4102a5059dca5a561d88c084778adb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">&#8220;Soil&#8221; represents the earth&#8217;s surface and is a critical medium within the study. It is being investigated in relation to greenhouse gas fluxes, specifically methane and nitrous oxide emissions. Soil plays a key role in carbon sequestration and the effects of crop residue return, as well as the impacts of no-tillage practices on aggregation and organic carbon. The study examines how soil influences soil carbon dioxide emissions, which are affected by factors like warming and waterlogging. Furthermore, &#8220;Soil&#8221; is the environment where microbial diversity, microbial biomass, and nematode populations are being studied, alongside earthworm activity and invertase and urease activities. The research investigates the effects of land-use change and global change factors on &#8220;Soil&#8221;, and how it regulates greenhouse gas fluxes, considering the influence of temperature and precipitation. Ultimately, &#8220;Soil&#8221; is the fundamental medium through which the study explores carbon assimilation, soil organic carbon stocks, and the overall dynamics of greenhouse gas fluxes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0169858f7671068d4573e925acb427d0,023f593be247e34a6ccb0b0773234348,09422e7ca0b65a42a71b6ab64427484f,0ae442eca4203831723b49d7c87ea06e,0bb7837f6ae9024c5b3b2fd42aaf1e0e,374df8372377d36a828795f6bed0dfd5,3be057a45b58e5c066d9f502879fc7e2,4caecf1d3bbc05db831098f8d95eeda3,5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b,62579b47cef9a431dfd75a35a7a302c9,65de24512bcf905100d1278cec81893e,7efa0b715bc3375cebd26b58040f5861,81f63213c44b6a3bf615b9e54ee71282,8ba70d47255b735ef718829891f70d44,962c4b2ae034cb1f11993dc22fd39589,9e4056573475eaed647bd42b3b7ee26f,b007ddcba413c3eaebd3f88aa1539d51,b42e797b1997ca97da0869c21842aeed,b4d1a20395e31d77608ee4c3ad9117a2,bbe0d857f7eb45611238b5595f62992d,c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea,c69f0e259b594afebd5f267ed27d0132,cab3d22bc19ec17273edff54c7610d1d,d1f1904224d30c046fea452f4ffd9353,d3a1a5449a3e98ee49b371d6db8ad57b,df8d03baf35fdc0eb054ebb4c7c0f592,e6b2446fd85a03b118b8c89c68039f50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Carbon is a key element, and a central focus of analysis, particularly concerning soil carbon stocks.</data>
      <data key="d2">4caecf1d3bbc05db831098f8d95eeda3,d197665d054f4591521b9d36fed232ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREENHOUSE GAS EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Greenhouse Gas Emissions refers to the emissions that are being reduced through sustainable production and are a key outcome of nitrogen enrichment, contributing to global warming. This concept is central to environmental concerns and is the primary outcome being investigated in the study, focusing on the specific environmental factor being investigated through cropland management practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e337c2de3d2bb087c4685e27f339750,4caecf1d3bbc05db831098f8d95eeda3,4ee7f805d2d16dca1ed7e775c4fe7943,715f5a401e83bc6bbd5f502a42378d1c,989334ecf6b07f4f972ca2440fead123,a7ca3157f97e89d28500ebf0febba8fb,b26f6d1927d82fdfcb201012ccff4244</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WETLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Wetlands are among the most important ecosystems in the response strategy to climate change. Furthermore, Wetlands are the subject of a study focused on carbon sequestration rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">562d18b67dffda4ce731674d1778ab05,c13bbffb2971415d2fb2b18723baf82a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON SEQUESTRATION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon Sequestration Rate is the key metric being investigated in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">c13bbffb2971415d2fb2b18723baf82a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAN ANNUAL TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Mean Annual Temperature is a significant factor influencing carbon sequestration rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc,c13bbffb2971415d2fb2b18723baf82a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNUAL PRECIPITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Annual Precipitation is another crucial factor affecting carbon sequestration rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">c13bbffb2971415d2fb2b18723baf82a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogen is a key element influencing nematode abundance, particularly in relation to nitrogen application rates. It is also identified as the primary factor controlling carbon sequestration rates. Furthermore, Nitrogen refers to the element that is a key component of ammonia and a major contributor to ammonia emissions.</data>
      <data key="d2">685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603,8ba70d47255b735ef718829891f70d44,c13bbffb2971415d2fb2b18723baf82a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASSAVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CROP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cassava is a major staple crop and crucial for food security in many countries of the world."</data>
      <data key="d2">eb87782bf2337238a5f1ba9db9b002c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD SECURITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food Security is a key concern due to the vulnerability of crops like cassava to pests and diseases."</data>
      <data key="d2">eb87782bf2337238a5f1ba9db9b002c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PESTS AND DISEASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pests and Diseases are a significant threat to cassava production, causing over 30% yield loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">eb87782bf2337238a5f1ba9db9b002c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFRICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Africa is the geographical region where the effects of climate-smart agriculture are being studied. Furthermore, Africa is the region where cassava production is projected to vary under 2030 climate projections.</data>
      <data key="d2">008784376aa194514362825aff81f709,eb87782bf2337238a5f1ba9db9b002c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2030 CLIMATE PROJECTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2030 Climate Projections represent a key factor influencing cassava production and vulnerability to pests and diseases."</data>
      <data key="d2">eb87782bf2337238a5f1ba9db9b002c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROUS OXIDE (N2O)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrous oxide (N2O) is a greenhouse gas that contributes to global warming. This description is consistent with multiple sources, highlighting its role as a significant contributor to global warming.</data>
      <data key="d2">01a9da175e36e03b278977a400f1bb32,069b2dcf04bff38a16d9925cf81fc318</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SONS LTD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sons Ltd is the organization being discussed in the review question."</data>
      <data key="d2">c8ac541681871dc581409deb26d81bd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL CARBON STOCKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Soil Carbon Stocks refers to the total amount of carbon stored within the soil.</data>
      <data key="d2">1248b50116da433fb3bdbe22e447b016,568ca7c7adca59277c002649461a2b67,75e6914d9b7ac58b0898b8eb12150b22,d197665d054f4591521b9d36fed232ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGROECOLOGICAL REGIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agroecological Regions refers to different geographical areas with specific environmental conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">75e6914d9b7ac58b0898b8eb12150b22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOREST-AGROFOREST-AGRICULTURE/PASTURE CONTINUUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Forest-Agroforest-Agriculture/Pasture continuum refers to the different land use systems being studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">75e6914d9b7ac58b0898b8eb12150b22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AFS refers to the specific agricultural system being investigated."</data>
      <data key="d2">75e6914d9b7ac58b0898b8eb12150b22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA, DAVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of California, Davis" is the institution conducting research on nitrogen retention strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">49f2b5b996654c3316dd13343d921a3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERRESTRIAL PLANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terrestrial Plants refers to the plants that are being studied in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phenology refers to the study of plant life cycles and their responses to environmental factors, including temperature."</data>
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Temperature is a critical environmental factor being studied in relation to various biological processes. Specifically, it influences soil greenhouse gas fluxes, the responsiveness of invertase and urease activities, plant phenology &#8211; particularly the length of the flowering season, and leaf litter decomposition rates. Furthermore, Temperature is recognized as a key factor influenced by greenhouse gas emissions, necessitating mitigation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f78616e6b65c9d016f9135e80758760,294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc,65de24512bcf905100d1278cec81893e,b42e797b1997ca97da0869c21842aeed,bbe0d857f7eb45611238b5595f62992d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOWERING SEASON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flowering Season is the length of time during which plants produce flowers, which is affected by experimental warming."</data>
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENTAL WARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Experimental Warming is a process used to study the effects of increased temperature on various biological systems. Specifically, it involves experimental warming treatments to investigate the responses of extracellular enzyme activities (EEA) and to assess the impact on terrestrial biomass. Furthermore, Experimental Warming is utilized to study plant phenology, examining how changes in temperature influence plant development cycles.</data>
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc,8c6fb9f4ceb04192e8f10369d1e43c30,965a77f3397728b22cc3186a77e62131</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATITUDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAN ANNUAL PRECIPITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">294c1904ead3cf55428108c98b152cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN DISTURBANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Human Disturbance refers to the activities of humans that impact dryland ecosystems. Specifically, it encompasses the impact of human activities on the environment, with a particular focus on inhibiting non-symbiotic nitrogen fixation within these ecosystems.</data>
      <data key="d2">96f967df08626506f57f19ca01d158d8,b72a6a5c25259e423b82dbf6df35b39a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN WILEY &amp; SONS LTD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"John Wiley &amp; Sons Ltd is the publisher of the research paper."</data>
      <data key="d2">88f3a4167997552f0ada4d0d6f78bf67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH PAPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The research paper examines several significant environmental challenges. Specifically, it investigates crop residue management, the effects of ocean acidification on marine fish physiological systems, and the impact of human disturbance and climate change on nitrogen fixation.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cfd64349725520c76be18f9e0f70ef8,88f3a4167997552f0ada4d0d6f78bf67,d571bc31d3ad957b2a55bc4f81b4936d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN FIXATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen Fixation refers to the process of converting atmospheric nitrogen into a usable form for plants."</data>
      <data key="d2">88f3a4167997552f0ada4d0d6f78bf67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plants are the primary beneficiaries of nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">88f3a4167997552f0ada4d0d6f78bf67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL CHANGE SCENARIOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global Change Scenarios are the context in which nitrogen fixation is being studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">88f3a4167997552f0ada4d0d6f78bf67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN DISTURBANCE ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">88f3a4167997552f0ada4d0d6f78bf67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANT BIOMASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plant biomass refers to the total mass of living organisms in a given area."</data>
      <data key="d2">5582d489a165c7ef5c2e0b725e609500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRRIGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Irrigation is a process of supplying water to plants."</data>
      <data key="d2">5582d489a165c7ef5c2e0b725e609500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DROUGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drought is a period of abnormally low rainfall."</data>
      <data key="d2">5582d489a165c7ef5c2e0b725e609500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agriculture is the primary source of ammonia emissions, impacting ecosystems and human health."</data>
      <data key="d2">02fc4190cd94078ab24614f9219074ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLUE-GREEN SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blue-green space" refers to the integration of water bodies and green spaces for urban cooling and mitigation of the urban heat island effect."</data>
      <data key="d2">63aa00e5162125efe3bc69a64877e80b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAND DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Land Degradation is the event that decreases the soil CH4 uptake rate."</data>
      <data key="d2">11dd17f53581012c609418f5a3c1221f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENRICHMENT PLANTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enrichment Planting is a management intervention that enhances C sequestration and minimizes GHG emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">d000c8cace1a850418d0863c2f04d370</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iran is the country where the study is conducted and the effects of climate change on malaria are investigated."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d852271fb314f043662b1220c601a23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROPICAL FORESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Tropical Forests refers to the geographical location where the study is conducted. Specifically, it encompasses forests found in Asia. The study focuses on a specific type of forest being investigated for climate change impacts, and the location of the study is within tropical forests.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e9c51f0e77cb7de623b5321b1975f1f,62ecd57f51a4e1b61952b3559585e920,823c08dda0ef4bfee3fc54f016f7144e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Asia is the geographical region being studied in the context of climate change impacts on tropical forests. Specifically, the tropical forests within this region are the focus of the study.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e9c51f0e77cb7de623b5321b1975f1f,823c08dda0ef4bfee3fc54f016f7144e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROPICAL TREES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tropical Trees refers to the tree species that are at risk of extinction due to climate change."</data>
      <data key="d2">0e9c51f0e77cb7de623b5321b1975f1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOREST POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Forest Policy refers to the management strategies that need to be integrated with climate change risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">0e9c51f0e77cb7de623b5321b1975f1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOREST POLICY AND MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Forest Policy and Management refers to the strategies and approaches being considered to address the climate change risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">823c08dda0ef4bfee3fc54f016f7144e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">China is a country where a wide range of studies are being conducted, encompassing carbon dynamics, farm management practices, and soil-crop system management. Specifically, research is focused on understanding the impacts of global warming on rice and wheat yields, the effects of elevated temperature on biomass, and the influence of organic conservation agriculture. Studies are also investigating the effects of manure, fertilizer management practices, and grazing on soil carbon and methane uptake. Furthermore, China is the location of national-scale data analysis, meta-analysis studies, and research into agricultural ammonia emissions and food demand. The country is experiencing challenges related to these issues, and experimental warming and N enrichment experiments are being conducted within China to assess their impacts.</data>
      <data key="d2">00f3b656d370c566e78f70da5f161986,20dfa37fd87f41ee23fc67db9fc1db33,24e771cb9389a57438330b1acd1f3294,2d43a3e995bc703bec05fa764a385653,31a7d9685ff84949e1e8412116f4ee1a,33b599f788dfcbca727a5db979017f62,509437fdaea77a93d1d86ab870462780,56587261f1750a09b6ff3a114b55eea2,577fac57e04724c04f04126c5f455de0,635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9,7d51439bc9bedf9979213cbb135fc9cb,8c6fb9f4ceb04192e8f10369d1e43c30,93b16693fca642d8a3c65c4383a93fc8,98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40,a917a6ee233e92cdd4520465577c4957,bce1ef8b9d353640835231850fd25a53,c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56,e6b2446fd85a03b118b8c89c68039f50,ff3530e1ce881ca26ebf5a179d958f22,ff7509bda4988f0946464abc1af71ff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC CONSERVATION AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organic Conservation Agriculture is the agricultural practice being studied for its impact on ammonia emissions, crop yields, and nitrogen use efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMMONIA EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Ammonia Emissions refers to the reduction in emissions achieved through organic conservation agriculture. Furthermore, Ammonia Emissions are the target of the mitigation measures being investigated.</data>
      <data key="d2">c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56,c6fc5221bcb65c143bca7514013f5fbe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN USE EFFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen Use Efficiency refers to the improvement in nitrogen utilization achieved through organic conservation agriculture."</data>
      <data key="d2">c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN CHEMICAL SOCIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Chemical Society is the organization conducting the research and publishing the findings."</data>
      <data key="d2">c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Research encompasses the investigation and study of various phenomena. Specifically, research involves conducting studies, such as those related to climate change, and focuses on areas like soil methane uptake. It also includes the investigation of the effect of multiple independent factors on nitrous oxide emission factors, and the review and summarization of research activities.</data>
      <data key="d2">6e6f91e446a74b293f86577d41b4fd0a,ad994bf386f4348d5c7bbbcf27c5045b,b33933572f7fbe73576a50647016e980,b4d1a20395e31d77608ee4c3ad9117a2,c1c9805d4c74d2481d35a83541e7cc4e,c5e2ed865f3c3bdb5e2076089cc24f56,df202b57f5743a087c5ed52f8c0a01f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;META-ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Meta-analysis is a research method employed to synthesize findings from multiple studies across a variety of fields. Specifically, it has been utilized to assess ocean acidification and warming in Caribbean corals, quantify N&#8322;O emissions from vegetable crops, and analyze the effect of NT/RT on GHG emission. Furthermore, meta-analysis has been applied to investigate the impact of global change factors on microbial diversity, the effect of tree attributes and local climatic conditions on the time since death of coarse woody debris ranging in decomposition states, and the effects of ocean acidification on marine calcifiers. The method involves reviewing a substantial number of studies, such as a review of 1570 observations reported in 121 field-based studies worldwide, to draw conclusions and ultimately quantify complex relationships.</data>
      <data key="d2">2aa7fb936e61b67d245b44373a14b069,2f22262feac375365545b5ef978c6d47,30f9da39940066c5933294f28484f5ba,8d48bbfbf794e394deef29c12547cb3f,b007ddcba413c3eaebd3f88aa1539d51,c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea,e3c4800a89fd40114b42745c3913c502,f986b510f5b73124fd301c35234f09c3,fb8df9250e9586c1f121167becfb6052</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN WILEY &amp; SONS LTD.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"John Wiley &amp; Sons Ltd." is the publisher of the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">41a831b24d18c89790e00000a1f828a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COVER CROP MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cover Crop Management refers to the practice of using cover crops to manage soil health and reduce greenhouse gas emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">6c07d9521776adad297626e5f6515d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENT ADDITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrient Addition refers to the process of adding nutrients to the soil. This process has a significant impact on soil extracellular enzyme activities.</data>
      <data key="d2">abda80eba504d6eb74af56b968bdda51,ba983e94c0ec7e2272c556855e3a9512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL EXTRACELLULAR ENZYME ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil extracellular enzyme activities refers to the biochemical processes occurring in soil mediated by enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">abda80eba504d6eb74af56b968bdda51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOSYSTEM AND EARTH SYSTEM MODELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ecosystem and earth system models refers to the models used to study the interactions between living organisms and their environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">abda80eba504d6eb74af56b968bdda51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINIMUM TILLAGE SYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Minimum Tillage Systems" refers to the agricultural practice of reducing soil disturbance during planting and harvesting."</data>
      <data key="d2">522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL CARBON ACCUMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil Carbon Accumulation" is the process of increasing the amount of carbon stored in the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROPLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Croplands" refers to areas of land used for agricultural production."</data>
      <data key="d2">522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUE RETENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residue Retention" is the practice of leaving crop residues on the soil surface after harvest."</data>
      <data key="d2">522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOC STOCKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">489357f7d77d21e208a06c332667b572,522f33553f705fd8f06351c16e864d1b,8c6fb9f4ceb04192e8f10369d1e43c30,93b16693fca642d8a3c65c4383a93fc8,c3cee2a6dd9450226b75ca3858bc51ab,df8d03baf35fdc0eb054ebb4c7c0f592</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EAST ASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"East Asia is the geographical region where biocar application is being evaluated for nitrous oxide mitigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">01f1caac7f343837e94c9e59d7328f44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">BIOCAR refers to a substance or method utilized for mitigating nitrous oxide emissions. It is also the application of this substance to agricultural soils, a key factor in the study&#8217;s findings. Furthermore, BIOCAR is an organization involved in the study of soil greenhouse gas fluxes.</data>
      <data key="d2">01f1caac7f343837e94c9e59d7328f44,4c4d4d735b12232890081f6bb215a34d,e1709f4cfffd2c8cec0303e08bbbf303</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROUS OXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrous Oxide is a chemical compound and a key component of the fluxes being studied. Specifically, it is the gas being emitted from soils, and its emission rate is influenced by soil pH. Furthermore, Nitrous Oxide is the substance being mitigated by biocar application.</data>
      <data key="d2">01f1caac7f343837e94c9e59d7328f44,81f63213c44b6a3bf615b9e54ee71282,833eeb09d91590901074cbaf07a6487a,b7140a24d3174f5132539645c9d54d87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCAR APPLICATION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biocar Application Rate is the rate at which biocar is applied, which is a key factor in the mitigation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">01f1caac7f343837e94c9e59d7328f44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UPLANDS SOILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Uplands Soils is the type of soil where biocar application is being evaluated."</data>
      <data key="d2">01f1caac7f343837e94c9e59d7328f44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N2O MITIGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">01f1caac7f343837e94c9e59d7328f44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAND-USE CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Land-Use Change is the primary driver of the study. It is defined as the transformation of land from one use to another and is being examined for its effects on soil fluxes.</data>
      <data key="d2">255f0842aee0aa59820fe7e3383ea6d4,c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL FLUXES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil Fluxes refers to the exchange of gases between the soil and the atmosphere, a key focus of the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">&#8220;Studies&#8221; refers to peer-reviewed papers used to investigate the responses of extracellular enzyme activities (EEA). The study utilizes a global meta-analysis of 62 studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">965a77f3397728b22cc3186a77e62131,c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global refers to the scope of the study, examining effects across the world."</data>
      <data key="d2">c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTHROPOCENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anthropocene refers to the current geological epoch defined by significant human impact on the planet."</data>
      <data key="d2">c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN-MANAGED ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Human-Managed Ecosystems represents the ecosystems transitioned to anthropogenic land use."</data>
      <data key="d2">c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natural Ecosystems represents the ecosystems that are being transitioned away from."</data>
      <data key="d2">c53bbe82c57666f6709c4e76605948ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUXES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluxes refers to the measurement of methane and nitrous oxide, indicating a scientific investigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">81f63213c44b6a3bf615b9e54ee71282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEEF MANAGEMENT STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Beef Management Strategies refer to changes in management practices used in beef production systems. Furthermore, these strategies encompass efforts to reduce greenhouse gas emissions from beef production.</data>
      <data key="d2">9495fb21bf504aa33170717a70028646,989334ecf6b07f4f972ca2440fead123</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEEF PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beef Production refers to the process of raising cattle for meat production."</data>
      <data key="d2">989334ecf6b07f4f972ca2440fead123</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL GHG EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global GHG Emissions refers to the total amount of greenhouse gases emitted worldwide."</data>
      <data key="d2">989334ecf6b07f4f972ca2440fead123</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORCHARD GRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Orchard Grass is a specific type of grass being studied for its impact on soil carbon."</data>
      <data key="d2">a917a6ee233e92cdd4520465577c4957</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL ORGANIC CARBON (SOC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Soil Organic Carbon (SOC) refers to the total amount of organic carbon stored within the soil. It represents the organic matter present in the soil.</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40,a917a6ee233e92cdd4520465577c4957,df8d03baf35fdc0eb054ebb4c7c0f592</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TILLAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tillage is a comparison point to orchard grass coverage, representing a traditional method of soil management."</data>
      <data key="d2">a917a6ee233e92cdd4520465577c4957</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOC&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">SOC, or Soil Organic Carbon, is a key metric in the review question.</data>
      <data key="d2">2095fe3380e39d8c278fd4a8bc815349,a917a6ee233e92cdd4520465577c4957</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMMONIA EMISSION REDUCTION STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ammonia Emission Reduction Strategies" refers to the various methods used to minimize ammonia emissions from agricultural systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGRICULTURAL SYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Agricultural Systems refers to the various farming systems where ammonia emission reduction strategies are implemented. These agricultural systems represent a key area of focus for these strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">3a2b00d2cc454d46a49d3a286f806746,685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertilizer" refers to the source of nitrogen that contributes to ammonia emissions when used in agricultural systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMMONIUM NITRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ammonium Nitrate" refers to a specific type of fertilizer that is particularly effective at reducing NH3 emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROLLED RELEASE FERTILIZER (CRF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEEP PLACEMENT OF FERTILIZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">685c8ba4d2b1e8da9d58fffd08c2a603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMISSION REDUCTION STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"emission reduction strategies" represents the strategies being considered to reduce emissions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3a2b00d2cc454d46a49d3a286f806746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMMONIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Ammonia is a chemical compound involved in the composting process and is also a specific environmental concern.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b2792c85ea69d4578b522fbffcc166a,3a2b00d2cc454d46a49d3a286f806746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSERVATION TILLAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Conservation Tillage is a Best Management Practice (BMP) that positively impacts soil health. Specifically, it is a CSA practice used to improve soil carbon sequestration and minimize soil disturbance. This approach also positively impacts soil organic carbon concentrations.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fbeb0764bb89c6e038be4536613f5ae,7462fd7b4621cabc6c52ab465dcec268,a16b2df06f38387a7858c4ce441036c5,cab3d22bc19ec17273edff54c7610d1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL NITROUS OXIDE EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil nitrous oxide emissions is the event being studied in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">cab3d22bc19ec17273edff54c7610d1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHELONIANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chelonians refers to turtles, a group of reptiles that are particularly vulnerable to climate change."</data>
      <data key="d2">fd80116ab9523ba9722fe86c6f42536c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Management refers to the proactive measures needed to mitigate the negative effects of climate change on Chelonians."</data>
      <data key="d2">fd80116ab9523ba9722fe86c6f42536c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORALLINE ALGAL COMMUNITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coralline algal communities are the subject of research regarding the impact of ocean acidification."</data>
      <data key="d2">5b764f991e98c00948fc9704042b0356</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REVIEW QUESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The &#8220;Review Question&#8221; represents a central inquiry being addressed across a range of research areas. Specifically, it encompasses questions related to climate warming and its impact on plant biomass. The &#8220;Review Question&#8221; also investigates management strategies concerning methane emissions from global ruminant agriculture systems, as well as the effects of nitrogen input on greenhouse gas emissions from wetland ecosystems. Furthermore, it examines the impact of land-use changes on soil organic carbon, the effects of tillage practices on soil and emissions, and the influence of elevated carbon dioxide on vegetable crop yields. The &#8220;Review Question&#8221; is also concerned with ocean acidification and its effects on coralline algal communities, and the effectiveness of 3-nitrooxypropanol as a feed additive for mitigating enteric methane emissions from ruminants. Finally, it addresses experimental soil warming and its consequences for soil carbon dynamics, and carbon assimilation and soil organic carbon stocks.</data>
      <data key="d2">000df0e8f7593fe58b852a7cd1c55576,0bb7837f6ae9024c5b3b2fd42aaf1e0e,190c3fbc40d9065edeac07be599bf865,2095fe3380e39d8c278fd4a8bc815349,374df8372377d36a828795f6bed0dfd5,71e94182f2792f04a9e245fe7d98bf53,7efa0b715bc3375cebd26b58040f5861,8677e194498b8a46cdf9b251ac571c78,9b6011d4cc513daf51a7204ab286c2f4,9df32b00727c80020064d71534042b5f,a43d06cacd8a24599d3c26ad86747a56,b7df5628d7a70d089969667fc888ec57,bf279f0c168f51dffd14bf76ce6f80b3,c67d047c45f8ba0a6e4722e26278e2b0,deddab81f28ca28f53a28825ce14d6ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYCORRHIZAL FUNGI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mycorrhizal fungi refers to a group of fungi that form symbiotic relationships with plant roots."</data>
      <data key="d2">ad00b210c704800774c7b6ff283cbed9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANT SPECIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plant species refers to the diverse range of plants that mycorrhizal fungi associate with."</data>
      <data key="d2">ad00b210c704800774c7b6ff283cbed9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Ecosystems refer to the different environments where soil C storage is being studied, and also the varied environments in which mycorrhizal fungi reside.</data>
      <data key="d2">568ca7c7adca59277c002649461a2b67,ad00b210c704800774c7b6ff283cbed9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Climate changes refers to the environmental shifts impacting mycorrhizal fungal&#8211;plant interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ad00b210c704800774c7b6ff283cbed9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHEAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CROP"</data>
      <data key="d1">Wheat is a major food crop and a staple crop that is experiencing impacts from climate change. Specifically, wheat production is seeing a reduction in protein concentrations, with grain protein levels decreasing by 5%-10% under elevated carbon dioxide conditions. It is important to note that &#8220;wheat&#8221; refers to a type of grain and is included in various analyses.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f,56587261f1750a09b6ff3a114b55eea2,5fddb03cbaea9cb313f7a263a982fa96,ac51de13c783140988c2e1b8cd8f0a0b,f2d2b392d684084e74377efb634eb891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPRINGER-VERLAG GMBH GERMANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Springer-Verlag GmbH Germany is the publisher of research findings and research papers.</data>
      <data key="d2">35b8fb79d3d9a06c9c96ff50990948dd,fbbd8d25c235c9c3b02bfa7bca87a80f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE AUTHOR(S)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">The Author(s) is the organization or person/group responsible for the research and the conclusions presented in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">35b8fb79d3d9a06c9c96ff50990948dd,7cd375966a161893a40e9c5813742fb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH FINDINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Research Findings refers to the study and its conclusions about climate action and ecosystem services."</data>
      <data key="d2">35b8fb79d3d9a06c9c96ff50990948dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATE ACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Climate Action refers to the strategies and measures taken to address climate change."</data>
      <data key="d2">35b8fb79d3d9a06c9c96ff50990948dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOSYSTEM SERVICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Ecosystem Services refer to the benefits that humans derive from natural ecosystems. These services are impacted by the loss of insect populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">35b8fb79d3d9a06c9c96ff50990948dd,d324615abd703fc0a45eaea837c41419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">35b8fb79d3d9a06c9c96ff50990948dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERRESTRIAL ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Terrestrial Ecosystems refers to ecosystems that exist on land, encompassing a variety of environments such as forests, grasslands, and deserts. Furthermore, the term &#8220;Terrestrial Ecosystems&#8221; indicates the geographical context of a study or observation, focusing on ecosystems found on land.</data>
      <data key="d2">1333043c14eff637016e6ecb92fa2dd0,60cb1f61e096039b21c2e02f5d416961,f873f5242e8445356a15260074522ac1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELEVATED GLOBAL ATMOSPHERIC CO2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elevated Global Atmospheric CO2 refers to the specific environmental condition being investigated, representing a key variable in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">1333043c14eff637016e6ecb92fa2dd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELSEVIER B.V.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Elsevier B.V. is a publishing organization responsible for the publication of research. Specifically, Elsevier B.V. is the publishing company conducting the review and that released the study, thereby indicating its source and credibility. It is recognized as the publisher of the research.</data>
      <data key="d2">1333043c14eff637016e6ecb92fa2dd0,6e6f91e446a74b293f86577d41b4fd0a,8677e194498b8a46cdf9b251ac571c78,b33933572f7fbe73576a50647016e980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The term &#8220;Study&#8221; refers to research conducted across several areas related to land-use change and its impacts. Specifically, &#8220;Study&#8221; encompasses research investigating the effects of land-use change on soil properties, the impacts of grazing on soil greenhouse gas fluxes, the effect of multiple independent factors on nitrous oxide emission factors, and the influence of elevated CO2 on plant stoichiometry.</data>
      <data key="d2">1333043c14eff637016e6ecb92fa2dd0,255f0842aee0aa59820fe7e3383ea6d4,962c4b2ae034cb1f11993dc22fd39589,ad994bf386f4348d5c7bbbcf27c5045b</data>
    </node>
