      <data key="d2">20dfa37fd87f41ee23fc67db9fc1db33,7d51439bc9bedf9979213cbb135fc9cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILIZATION MEASURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertilization Measures refers to the application of fertilizers to the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">7d51439bc9bedf9979213cbb135fc9cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Climate refers to the weather conditions in a specific region. It is a factor that influences the effectiveness of CSA practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d51439bc9bedf9979213cbb135fc9cb,a16b2df06f38387a7858c4ce441036c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC FERTILIZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organic Fertilizers refers to the application of organic materials to the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">7d51439bc9bedf9979213cbb135fc9cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAW RETURN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Straw Return refers to the practice of returning straw to the soil. It involves the return of straw to the soil.</data>
      <data key="d2">20dfa37fd87f41ee23fc67db9fc1db33,7d51439bc9bedf9979213cbb135fc9cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLICY MEASURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Policy Measures refers to the measures taken to accurately reflect the effects of soil carbon storage."</data>
      <data key="d2">20dfa37fd87f41ee23fc67db9fc1db33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROPLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cropland is the type of land where the study on soil carbon storage is being conducted."</data>
      <data key="d2">20dfa37fd87f41ee23fc67db9fc1db33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILIZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertilizers refers to the substances used to improve soil quality."</data>
      <data key="d2">20dfa37fd87f41ee23fc67db9fc1db33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N FERTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">N fertilization refers to the event of applying synthetic nitrogen fertilizer to agricultural soils.</data>
      <data key="d2">ade2222bf4436447f6a52c3768b1e61b,b7140a24d3174f5132539645c9d54d87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGRICULTURAL SOILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Agricultural Soils are the subject of extensive study and measurement, particularly concerning nitrous oxide emissions. These soils serve as the location where nitrogen-enriched biocarbons, including animal manure and biochar, are applied and where the effects of nitrogen fertilization are being investigated. Specifically, Agricultural Soils are the target environment for biocar applications and are being monitored to understand their influence on nitrous oxide emissions. Furthermore, research into the effects of antibiotics and the broader impact of nitrogen fertilization on these soils is also conducted. In essence, Agricultural Soils represent the land where crops are grown and where the overall impact of various agricultural practices on nitrous oxide emissions is analyzed.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e710a1cdb43db1d599344c87b056d15,27e0bbe91c2a1c1dde27e277dc76aafd,2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7,3f0baab0a092b73c19b840228559486e,4c4d4d735b12232890081f6bb215a34d,5da7d887d733f9d47863aa0adc13aabf,6e6f91e446a74b293f86577d41b4fd0a,858061fa9414cf3c62757890ca9aac4f,9167ad08493be3198ea3e4afc4699c69,b7140a24d3174f5132539645c9d54d87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN FERTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogen fertilization is being investigated for its impact on soil processes. It is defined as the process of adding nitrogen to agricultural soils. Furthermore, nitrogen fertilization plays a role in regulating the response of GWP to mid-season drainage.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7,9167ad08493be3198ea3e4afc4699c69,960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL DENITRIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil Denitrification" is the key process affected by nitrogen fertilization, showing exponential increases at lower fertilizer rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL N2O EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil N2O Emissions" are linked to denitrification, with a small decrease in the N2O:N-2 ratio when combined with organic fertilizer."</data>
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N2O:N-2 RATIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N2O:N-2 Ratio" is a measure of the balance between nitrous oxide and nitrogen gas, influenced by denitrification."</data>
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC FERTILIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organic Fertilizer" is used in conjunction with synthetic N fertilizer to reduce N2O emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N2O EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">N2O Emissions refers to the emission of nitrous oxide from forest soils. The event being influenced by nitrogen management practices is N2O Emissions.</data>
      <data key="d2">20f5e5ee934896ff3832296717da98c8,2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7,85eab0ae626d402f5775b96efd661475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNTHETIC N FERTILIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL CLAY CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">2f4a6b1ed3296f6deec235872b1aedf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROUS OXIDE EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrous Oxide Emissions refers to the event of measuring and quantifying the release of nitrous oxide gas from agricultural soils. It is a specific event or process being investigated, focusing on the increase in emissions due to elevated carbon dioxide, and is fundamentally linked to nitrogen management practices. Ultimately, Nitrous Oxide Emissions represents a specific environmental impact &#8211; the measured release of nitrous oxide from agricultural fields.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e710a1cdb43db1d599344c87b056d15,20f5e5ee934896ff3832296717da98c8,2cfd64349725520c76be18f9e0f70ef8,62ecd57f51a4e1b61952b3559585e920,858061fa9414cf3c62757890ca9aac4f,9167ad08493be3198ea3e4afc4699c69,bdec452dc57b933b0d09901322d3d306,d8644b355255c3ebadd9376940f9aff1,df2c9388abcb63b3adc216c218461096,e6b2446fd85a03b118b8c89c68039f50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROUS OXIDE:N2 RATIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrous oxide:N2 ratio refers to the ratio of nitrous oxide to nitrogen gas in agricultural soils."</data>
      <data key="d2">9167ad08493be3198ea3e4afc4699c69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Rice refers to a type of grain and is a major food crop included in the analysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f,56587261f1750a09b6ff3a114b55eea2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOYBEAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"soybean" is a major food crop included in the analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIELD PEAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"field peas" is a major food crop included in the analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"corn" is a major food crop included in the analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;META-ANALYSIS STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"meta-analysis studies" refers to the studies analyzed in the research."</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREE-AIR [CO2] ENRICHMENT (FACE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"free-air [CO2] enrichment (FACE)" is a research method used to study the effects of elevated carbon dioxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPORTING BIAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"reporting bias" is a factor considered in the analysis of meta-analysis studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">4e73e33e626223341dbd87cc10bc9d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROPICAL AGROFORESTRY ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tropical agroforestry ecosystems refers to a specific geographic area or type of ecosystem."</data>
      <data key="d2">0388bb5a38bfd002bb35bcf4473024e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VEGETABLE PRODUCTION SYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vegetable Production Systems are the systems being affected by climate change."</data>
      <data key="d2">fcaf7506797fe15f7c0168be7d966591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAULIFLOWER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cauliflower is a specific vegetable affected by temperature changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">fcaf7506797fe15f7c0168be7d966591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature Changes are the key factor causing issues with cauliflower head induction."</data>
      <data key="d2">fcaf7506797fe15f7c0168be7d966591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD INDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head Induction is the process affected by temperature changes in cauliflower."</data>
      <data key="d2">fcaf7506797fe15f7c0168be7d966591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2015/16 EL NINO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2015/16 El Nino event is a significant climate event that caused widespread coral bleaching."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORAL BLEACHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coral Bleaching is a widespread event caused by El Nino events."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
      <data key="d3">"EVENT"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EL NINO SOUTHERN OSCILLATION (ENSO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"El Nino Southern Oscillation (ENSO) is a climate event that causes coral bleaching."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORAL REEFS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">Coral Reefs are the target of a study. They are underwater ecosystems built by colonies of coral polyps and are experiencing warming and bleaching as a geographical feature.</data>
      <data key="d2">021184116f0e8f18db4bc77e0d56aacf,3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad,68b27597321e63998690804d3744af35</data>
      <data key="d3">"GEO"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGREE HEATING WEEKS (DHW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degree Heating Weeks (DHW) is a method for quantifying coral heat stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMOTELY-SENSED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remotely-Sensed refers to the method of quantifying coral heat stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL CORAL REEF SYMPOSIUM (ICRS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"International Coral Reef Symposium (ICRS) is a source of data for the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL CLIMATE CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global Climate Change is a driver of coral bleaching."</data>
      <data key="d2">3cffb039e111c6130d1510f047dc27ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOESS PLATEAU OF CHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Loess Plateau of China is the geographical location of the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXED-SPECIES PLANTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mixed-species plantations are the type of plantation being studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOCULTURE PLANTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monoculture plantations are the type of plantation being studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL TOTAL NITROGEN (STN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"STN refers to the total amount of nitrogen in the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATE-LIMITED REGIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Climate-limited regions are the geographical locations where the mixed-species plantations were more effective."</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABANDONED LAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abandoned land is the type of land where afforestation was conducted."</data>
      <data key="d2">98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFFORESTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Afforestation is the process of planting trees, representing a significant environmental initiative. It is being studied for its effects on soil methane fluxes and is defined as the type of event being studied, particularly in the context of restoring degraded land.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c748894d4bdf8793fb7aba4cfaa5017,98b6614bc93b7e3ed9bf4f40f3e0be40,d1f1904224d30c046fea452f4ffd9353</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SR REFERS TO THE SUBSTITUTION RATIO OF MANURE TO SYNTHETIC FERTILIZER."</data>
      <data key="d1">7)("entity"</data>
      <data key="d2">273547d29b496aee6f2a8540f2647d66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Manure is animal waste that is utilized as fertilizer. Specifically, the application of manure significantly reduces nitrous oxide emissions from leafy vegetables.</data>
      <data key="d2">571c7c084a2abb1e316c716212d59049,635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Emissions refers to the release of substances into the environment. This includes the release of gases into the atmosphere, such as greenhouse gases like CH4 and N2O.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e337c2de3d2bb087c4685e27f339750,635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9,960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NH3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NH3 refers to ammonia, a component of manure."</data>
      <data key="d2">635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N2O refers to nitrous oxide, a greenhouse gas."</data>
      <data key="d2">635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CH4 refers to methane, a greenhouse gas."</data>
      <data key="d2">635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PADDY RICE SOILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paddy Rice Soils refers to the type of soil where manure is being applied."</data>
      <data key="d2">635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABATEMENT STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abatement Strategies refers to methods for reducing emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">635ba10bbfd9103c7f7c995ae28670d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILIZER MANAGEMENT PRACTICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertilizer Management Practices refers to the application of fertilizer, which is a key factor in the study of crop productivity and soil carbon sequestration."</data>
      <data key="d2">24e771cb9389a57438330b1acd1f3294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROP PRODUCTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Crop Productivity refers to the yield of crops, which is a key outcome of fertilizer management practices. It is also defined as the outcome being measured in the study of climate-smart agriculture management.</data>
      <data key="d2">008784376aa194514362825aff81f709,24e771cb9389a57438330b1acd1f3294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BMOF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BMOF is a specific fertilizer management practice being studied and its impacts are assessed."</data>
      <data key="d2">24e771cb9389a57438330b1acd1f3294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRIP-IRRIGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drip-Irrigation" is a specific irrigation system that is being compared to other systems in terms of its impact on nitrous oxide emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">0e710a1cdb43db1d599344c87b056d15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FURROW AND SPRINKLER IRRIGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Furrow and Sprinkler Irrigation" represents the comparison group for drip-irrigation in terms of nitrous oxide emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">0e710a1cdb43db1d599344c87b056d15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICE FIELDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rice Fields are the location where the study is conducted, influencing the emissions and yields."</data>
      <data key="d2">960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MID-SEASON DRAINAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mid-Season Drainage is a key factor affecting emissions and yields in rice fields."</data>
      <data key="d2">960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH4 AND N2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CH4 and N2O are greenhouse gases that are being studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN FERTILIZATION APPLICATION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen Fertilization Application Rate is a specific parameter that influences the emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAIN YIELD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grain Yield is a measure of productivity in rice fields."</data>
      <data key="d2">960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC MATTER AMENDMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">960ea94aa2f23a9383700b5ebd430baa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL CARBON CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil Carbon Content refers to the amount of carbon stored in the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">568ca7c7adca59277c002649461a2b67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiments are needed to further investigate the processes of soil C storage."</data>
      <data key="d2">568ca7c7adca59277c002649461a2b67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LITTER INPUTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Litter Inputs refers to the amount of organic material added to the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">568ca7c7adca59277c002649461a2b67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RANDOM FOREST (RF) MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MODEL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Random Forest (RF) model was used to analyze the impacts of NT on soil aggregation and SOC."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATIC CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL FACTOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Climatic Conditions were identified as a key factor influencing changes in soil aggregation and SOC under NT."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENTAL DURATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL FACTOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experimental Duration was identified as a key factor influencing changes in soil aggregation and SOC under NT."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL TEXTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL FACTOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">Soil Texture refers to the physical properties of the soil, which is a key factor influencing the treatment effects. Soil Texture was identified as a key factor influencing changes in soil aggregation and Soil Organic Carbon (SOC) under NT conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b,dd3ae0347fbac763d15e83b9ca92968f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INITIAL SOC/PH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL FACTOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial SOC/pH was identified as a key factor influencing changes in soil aggregation and SOC under NT."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NO-TILLAGE (NT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"No-tillage (NT) is the agricultural practice being studied for its impact on soil aggregation and SOC."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL TILLAGE (CT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conventional Tillage (CT) is the agricultural practice being compared to No-tillage (NT)."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL AGGREGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Soil aggregation refers to the physical structure of soil, and more specifically, the process of soil particles binding together to form aggregates. No-tillage practices have been shown to increase soil aggregation by 49%, 11%, and 23%.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b,d3a1a5449a3e98ee49b371d6db8ad57b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGGREGATE-ASSOCIATED SOIL ORGANIC CARBON (SOC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aggregate-associated Soil Organic Carbon (SOC) refers to the organic carbon stored within soil aggregates."</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON SEQUESTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Carbon Sequestration is the primary outcome being investigated in the experiment. Specifically, it refers to the process of capturing and storing atmospheric carbon dioxide.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b,8c53e8851555696d99aa9e7d9e102abe,c69f0e259b594afebd5f267ed27d0132</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC CARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Organic Carbon refers to carbon that exists in a combined, organic chemical form. Furthermore, it represents the amount of carbon stored in the soil, a factor significantly influenced by no-tillage practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d15d6937c12266566ee7ac1e70a4d6b,d3a1a5449a3e98ee49b371d6db8ad57b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NO-TILLAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">No-tillage is a farming practice that significantly impacts soil aggregation and organic carbon levels. Furthermore, it is a soil conservation practice recognized for its ability to reduce greenhouse gas emissions and provide yield benefits.</data>
      <data key="d2">6eea6409f7f381a11b35a1e7d53fe670,d3a1a5449a3e98ee49b371d6db8ad57b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URBAN HEAT ISLAND (UHI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urban Heat Island (UHI) refers to the phenomenon of higher temperatures in urban areas compared to surrounding rural areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">82b9f32cbeecdac49a30d21ccad5afa1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL INVERTASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil invertase refers to an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of sucrose."</data>
      <data key="d2">a04c96e2200c21a441b87c19594636ae</data>
    </node>
