    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Biodiversity refers to the variety of life on Earth, and is threatened by extreme climate events. It also represents the overall measure of the impact of climate change on pollinators.</data>
      <data key="d2">40779d37dc6109c75c8ee8b81e777ffd,d324615abd703fc0a45eaea837c41419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANT PHENOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Plant phenology is the scientific study of the timing of plant life cycle events. It encompasses the observation and analysis of events such as leaf emergence and flowering within plant life cycles.</data>
