    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OCEAN ACIDIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Ocean Acidification refers to the decrease in the pH value of the world&#8217;s oceans and other large bodies of water. This process is caused by the uptake of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere, resulting in a reduction of the ocean&#8217;s pH.</data>
      <data key="d2">021184116f0e8f18db4bc77e0d56aacf,299098521a698233902ae7feb361856c,417da0bb0172320162de784173653a16,d571bc31d3ad957b2a55bc4f81b4936d,e3c4800a89fd40114b42745c3913c502</data>
    </node>
