      <data key="d2">4c748894d4bdf8793fb7aba4cfaa5017</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANIMAL MANURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Animal Manure is a type of organic amendment that is applied to agricultural soils. It is utilized to regulate nitrous oxide emissions.</data>
      <data key="d2">27e0bbe91c2a1c1dde27e277dc76aafd,858061fa9414cf3c62757890ca9aac4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BICHAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Bichar is an organic amendment utilized to regulate nitrous oxide emissions. It is applied to agricultural soils, directly influencing the levels of nitrous oxide emitted from these lands.</data>
      <data key="d2">27e0bbe91c2a1c1dde27e277dc76aafd,858061fa9414cf3c62757890ca9aac4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL PH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Soil pH is a key edaphic factor that significantly influences various aspects of soil health. Specifically, it impacts the emission rate of nitrous oxide from soils and plays a role in regulating these emissions following the application of organic amendments. Furthermore, Soil pH is associated with influencing soil microbial diversity.</data>
      <data key="d2">27e0bbe91c2a1c1dde27e277dc76aafd,76b172515cd810e614844730c72e0644,b7140a24d3174f5132539645c9d54d87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL C: N RATIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil C: N Ratio" influences nitrous oxide emissions, with high ratios increasing emissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">27e0bbe91c2a1c1dde27e277dc76aafd</data>
    </node>
